  "type": "PARENT",
  "data": {
    "body": "Below we show a simplified model of a person's leg in cast that is pulled up by a sling. The leg and cast together is the system that is modeled as a rigid, uniform rod of mass \\textbf{m = 34 kg} and length \\textbf{L = 0.8 m} is attached to the body at a hinge at point \\textbf{A}. The leg and cast are lifted by the sling that exerts a vertical force of magnitude, \\textbf{F} which is applied at a distance, \\textbf{d = 0.56 m} from the 'hinge', to hold the leg at an angle $\\mathbf{\\theta}$ = $65^\\circ$ above the horizontal. Magnitude of acceleration due to gravity is $\\mathbf{g = 10   m/s^2}$.",
